en sent gail  dornick to terminus to set up the vault  after they were already there the big  change on the show is that the vault is  on the planet when they arrive making it  mysterious and it hovers above the  surface emitting a null field that keeps  everyone but salvor from approaching it  in the books it's just basically a  chamber everyone knows that gail dornick  came there and installed it and that  something's going to happen on the 50th  anniversary the show moved things up a  bit to 35 years after they got there but  you have to guess that it was still  placed there by harry somehow and the  opening is still part of where the  show's heading  salvor is the warden instead of the  mayor and the whole idea of her  connection with it and being special  seems like they're blending a couple of  characters together that's what i'll  talk about at the end in the spoilers  section but here i'll just say that the  idea of some people being different or  special in foundation isn't as  antithetical as some people seem to  think that doesn't mean it's not jarring  to see salvor portrayed as more of a  warrior though i mentioned in my last  recap that it was a wtf moment when she  discredited the saying that violence is  the last refuge of the incompetent  that's the phrase the character is known  for and they relied more on their wit  than anything else it's still a bit too  early to tell if they're just setting up  a twist or if it's about the other part  of the character they've added to their  version of salvor though for that we'll  just have to wait and see  i also mentioned that i wish that they  would have developed the encyclopedias a  bit more mostly because there is a nice  tension with the way that they think and  what they're trying to do and what  salvor needs to figure out in order to  get through the crisis in the show they  changed things quite a bit by the  encyclopedist knowing what harry was  predicting in the books they knew he set  up the foundation that they were there  to collect this knowledge but not really  about how the empire was falling and how  they were going to be the ones who were  going to bring it back after the fall  that's only revealed to them over time  but when i thought about this some more  i guess the encyclopedists and what they  do reflects the bigger picture of why  the empire is failing and in the show  they just decided to show us the fall  through the genetic dynasty it's a  different way to get there but they  could still arrive in the same place so  those are the big things terminus is  more isolated it's a little earlier in  their development and acrion's coming  there with different motivations which  haven't been revealed yet the  encyclopedists are more of a mixed bag  they still rely on the idea of the  empire which is the same but they know  more about harry's predictions they  aren't waiting for the ball to open but  they are expecting that harry factored  in everything so there's no need to  worry they still have tension with  salvor but it's for different reasons i  don't care much about them removing the  idea of the decline of atomic power from  the periphery it wasn't the strongest  idea in the series but i do wonder how  things will change down the road as a  result so we'll see where it goes from  here now i'm going to talk about what i  think is going on with gail and salvore  and this is the part where i'm gonna  talk about book spoilers that might  spoil things for you if you haven't read  them all please like and subscribe on  your way out because this is your chance  to leave  by the end of the second episode it  seemed pretty clear that gail had  mentality powers at least the show's  version of what those will turn out to  be they made the character female put  her in a relationship with rach and that  produced a zygote that was put in  storage before she left in the escape  pod when you think of mentalix you think  of the second foundation which hasn't  been mentioned at all on the show yet  and when you think of rach's child you  think wanda selden the key mentality in  the second foundation's creation when  you combine that with salvor seeing  visions of rach coming from the vault it  seems pretty likely that she's their kid  and that her and gail are going to be  the genesis of the second foundation  there's plenty that isn't clear about  what harry knew or how he was involved  and that's why it's kind of frustrating  that they dropped that part of the story  for two episodes there's a lot of  questions after that in how things will  play out it doesn't really work if  salvor stays on terminus and who  actually knows which time period gayle  will wake up in there's also the outside  possibility that harry wasn't involved  at all in the show gail did say the math  was incomplete so maybe they're setting  it up that she wakes up and realizes  what's missing is the second foundation  it could go in a lot of different ways  but at least in broad strokes that seems  to be the direction they're headed with  them being special i'm curious to see  how that turns out and i think that's a  good place to leave things let me know  in the comments what you think just if  you're going to be talking about book  spoilers make sure you mark them please  like this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon

